<speak>I've done that now. The business notebook is closed, and I've put my phone face down. Here is the part I prepared for our call. The holding I want you to transact in is Pioneer Balanced Opportunities Fund. I want to sell that holding. I'll move to the next line in a moment. I wrote each item separately rather than squeezing everything into one sentence. That way I don't skip over something when I'm speaking. It also makes the page easier for me to use afterwards, without having to remember what a little arrow in the margin was supposed to mean.</speak>